                "name": "seedance-cinematic-prompter",
                "canonical_slug": null,
                "description": "How to write a Seedance 2.0 / 2.5 (or Sora, Veo, Kling) video prompt with the CINEDANCE prompt layer: decide the scene, then write the prompt yourself from its reference copies; the CINEDANCE writer, higgsfield_enhancer(flow=\"seedance-prompt\"), is optional for 30s+ sequences split into several generations or on request. Use when the user asks to write, fix or audit a Seedance prompt, after a failed or weak Seedance render, for a cinematic one-off clip, or to turn a supplied storyboard into one clip. Lazy input (\"epic sci-fi scene\") means you invent the scene first; only when the user explicitly hands the content to the video model does the call use mode \"random\". For a one-off anime or stylized scene, decide the look and scene yourself and use this; stylized-animation is for full multi-clip productions. Not for genre workflows with their own skills (UGC, podcast, motion design, ads), not for editing or re-angling existing footage (video-reangler), not for MiniMax H3 or Gemini Omni workflows.",
